# A data-property disjointness is inert when one side is idle: emptying that
# property satisfies it. Between two used properties it stays omitted, as do
# the assertions that use them. INCONCLUSIVE (exit 2).

@prefix :     <http://example.org/t#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

<http://example.org/t> a owl:Ontology .
:u1 a owl:DatatypeProperty .
:u2 a owl:DatatypeProperty .
:i  a owl:DatatypeProperty .
:u1 owl:propertyDisjointWith :i .
:u1 owl:propertyDisjointWith :u2 .
:a a owl:NamedIndividual ; :u1 1 ; :u2 2 .
